  "body": "https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/f41ba8d2530b4b252bb733a36f462bd983379fbb/#matching-an-image-type-pattern\r\n\r\n> Let the byte sequence to be matched be the byte sequence to be matched\\. \r\n\r\nIn her JSConf EU talk, @kosamari pointed out that this is a bit ridiculous. We can do better.\r\n\r\nThis spec is in general quite old and has not benefited from modern practices in spec-English, but maybe we can modernize the pattern matching algorithm and the invocations of it, as a first pass.\r\n\r\nIn particular, the pattern matching algorithm should have clearly delineated inputs with variable names, instead of some of them being implicit. And it shouldn't restate how byte sequences work (\"where mask[m] is byte m in mask and mask[0] is the first byte in mask\") repeatedly.",
